    "turn_text": "it is a huge message for republicans today uh... the reality is a couple different number one lots of activist republicans believe that all elections are decided on philosophy. The Trump followers right now who are most intense think it's all about philosophy and the reality is it's almost has almost nothing to do with philosophy. And I think I've said this before, lots of times people who get stoked up or become exercised or suddenly discover the nation is in danger and decide to become active, they're the last to figure out that elections are decided largely by human nature. I found it stunning and encouraging that when we first got to Washington, the class of 1995 or the class of 1984, the Newt Gingrich freshman, that Newt understood and Dick Army understood, and they would repeat to us over and over again, they, meaning voters, have to know how much you care before they'll care how much you know. And it actually works in two different ways. It works for the minimally involved who get all stoked up and think they can elect a candidate because he's a rock solid conservative. But if he's an unlikable, unappealing rock solid conservative, getting him elected is going to be extremely different. Look at Ronald Reagan versus You mentioned him the other day. The Republican who was run a million times and his sister was deeply involved.",
